    "explanation": "Both of you: the trip is TRP-00106, Toa Payoh to Bugis on 17 July 2026, and the charge in dispute is $26.04 (EV-TRIP-00106, EV-GPS-00106, EV-FARE-00106).\n\nThe deviation is established, and it is ESTABLISHED only. On the governing GPS trace (EV-GPS-00106, weight 1.0, COMPLETE) the trip ran 10.78 km against a booked optimal of 7.2 km (EV-TRIP-00106), an excess of 3.58 km = 49.72% of optimal. That clears both POL-RD-01 establishment tests (over 20% and over 0.8 km), so the driver's and the rider's POL-RD-01 claims are accepted. It clears neither materiality test (not over 50%, not over 8.0 km), so the deviation is not MATERIAL, and I use the trace figure, not the rounded 10.8 km trip_record copy. The trace is not impaired under POL-RD-07: 169 fixes at an unbroken 10-second interval, 100% coverage, no gaps, max inter-fix gap 0 s, so no independent corroboration is required and POL-RD-10(3) does not fire.\n\nNo exoneration applies. No traffic advisory covers the trip window — EV-ADVIS-00106-01 is MISSING, weight_multiplier 0.0, issue code MISSING_ARTIFACT — and neither party asserts an external traffic cause (the driver filed no counterparty_statement at all), so under POL-RD-13 the absent advisory is a gap in the bundle rather than a contradiction, POL-RD-03 is unavailable, and nothing reduces the measured excess. The single chat message (EV-CHAT-00106) is the rider's own complaint — 'why we at havelock? bugis is behind us' — not an instruction; its waypoint_hint is null, so POL-RD-04's corroboration test cannot be run and the clause is unavailable, and under POL-RD-14 the message excludes no distance. No pickup/dropoff amendment, a METERED fare (quoted_fare_sgd null) and a RYDE_TAXI vehicle leave POL-RD-05, POL-RD-11 and POL-RD-12 with nothing to run on. The rider's discharge of the initial burden under POL-RD-08 is accepted.\n\nThe refund is arithmetic under POL-RD-02. Charged total: $26.04. Recomputed fare: (3.80 base + 0.75 x 7.2 km = 5.40 + 0.28 x 19 min = 5.32) x 1.0 surge, read from EV-FARE-00106.surge_multiplier, plus 0.80 platform fee plus 0.00 ERP on the optimal route = $15.32. Refund = 26.04 - 15.32 = $10.72, above the $0.50 de minimis and rounded up to $10.75 payable. That is 41.2% of the charge, below the 90% POL-RD-02 requires for a full refund, so the rider's request for the whole $26.04 is refused.\n\nThe $5.50 of ERP is inside that $10.75, not added to it. Both gantries are genuine crossings of the corridor actually driven (the trace passes within 0.0 m and 24.1 m, inside the 250 m match radius), so there is no POL-RD-09(4) billing-integrity refund; but the recomputed fare contains no off-route gantry (optimal_route_erp_sgd 0.00), so the $5.50 is returned as part of the POL-RD-02 figure, and POL-RD-09(1) forbids charging it a second time. The $5.50 as a separate line, and the full $26.04, are both refused.\n\nNo repeat-deviation pattern is available: driver_profile.deviation_flags_90d is 0 against 96 completed trips, below both POL-RD-06 thresholds, so the balance-of-evidence tie-break, the FULL_REFUND uplift and the POL-RD-06(c) conduct referral all fall away. The lifetime counter prior_deviation_flags is context only under POL-GEN-01 and was not used as a ground. NO_ACTION would leave the rider carrying the whole $26.04 and is not the outcome the evidence supports.\n\nOutcome: PARTIAL_REFUND of $10.75 to the rider. No driver compensation is due — the billed 10.8 km is not less than the 10.78 km trace, so POL-RD-04's compensation limb has no shortfall to run on. Because the monetary effect exceeds the $8.00 execution threshold (POL-GEN-05), the amount is issued but held for release by a human reviewer. No referral fires on these facts. This ruling is consistent with precedents P-0001 and P-0002, which share its clauses."
  },
