    "explanation": "This ruling is addressed to both parties. ROUTE AND DEVIATION GRADE: The platform trace (EV-GPS-00106, weight 1.0, COMPLETE, 169 fixes at a 10-second interval with no gaps) measures the trip at 10.78 km against the booked optimal of 7.2 km (EV-TRIP-00106), an excess of 3.58 km — 49.72% of optimal. That clears both POL-RD-01 establishment tests (more than 0.8 km and more than 20% of optimal), so the deviation is ESTABLISHED. It does not clear the 50% or 8.0 km materiality gate, so it is not a MATERIAL deviation: no POL-RD-06 pattern check is required, no FULL_REFUND uplift is available, and there is no conduct referral. Both advocates agree on this and I accept it. In any event the driver's profile (deviation_flags_90d 0 against completed_trips_90d 96) meets neither limb of the POL-RD-06 test. THE FARE: The fare is METERED, so POL-RD-02 governs. recomputed_fare = (3.80 base + 0.75 x 7.2 km = 5.40 + 0.28 x 19.0 min = 5.32) x 1.0 surge, read from EV-FARE-00106.surge_multiplier, + 0.80 platform fee + 0.00 on-optimal-route ERP = 15.32. Charged_total is 26.04. Refund = 26.04 - 15.32 = 10.72, which rounds UP to a payable of SGD 10.75. That is 41.2% of the charge, below the 90% that would promote it to a full refund, so the outcome is PARTIAL_REFUND. ERP: The $5.50 of ERP across the two CTE gantries is ALREADY comprehended in that refund — the recomputed fare rebuilds the trip on a route with no gantry (optimal_route_erp_sgd 0.00) — and POL-RD-09(1) forbids adding off-route ERP on top of the POL-RD-02 figure. Both gantries are genuine crossings (the trace passes 0.0 m and 24.1 m from them), so no billing-integrity referral under POL-RD-09(4) arises. TRACE INTEGRITY: EV-GPS-00106 is not impaired for policy purposes under POL-RD-07 (no 90-second gap, no 500 m jump, no sustained interval above 30 seconds), so the deviation stands on the trace alone and no POL-RD-10(3) escalation applies. CHAT: The single message (EV-CHAT-00106, rider, 08:46:30) is a complaint — 'why we at havelock? bugis is behind us' — not an instruction; waypoint_hint is null and no road is named, so POL-RD-04 is unavailable and no distance is excluded. TRAFFIC: No advisory covers this trip window (EV-ADVIS-00106-01 is MISSING, weight 0.0, issue MISSING_ARTIFACT) and the driver has asserted no external traffic cause (no counterparty statement on file). Under POL-RD-13 the absent advisory cannot reduce the measured excess; it is a gap in the bundle, not a POL-RD-10(5) contradiction, and it does not escalate the case. DRIVER COMPENSATION: None is due; the rider was billed 10.8 km against a 10.78 km trace, so there is no unbilled shortfall under POL-RD-04. EXECUTION: The monetary effect (SGD 10.75) exceeds the POL-GEN-05 execution threshold of SGD 8.00, so this provisional ruling issues but is not executed automatically — the amount is held and the case is placed in the human release queue. That gating does not change the ruling. One rider claim (that the burden had shifted and no exculpatory clause could run) was discarded at the citation stage for citing the missing advisory without naming its issue code; it appears in the audit list and is not relied on. Earlier PARTIAL_REFUND precedents sharing these clauses match this outcome; nothing in this case's evidence distinguishes them."
  },
