    "explanation": "Both accounts of the arithmetic agree on this record, and it supports a partial refund to the rider.\n\nDeviation (POL-RD-01). The governing trace distance is 10.78 km (EV-GPS-00106, weight 1.0) against a booked optimal of 7.2 km from the trip record (EV-TRIP-00106), an excess of 3.58 km — 49.72% of optimal. Both establishment limbs pass (the excess is above the 0.8 km absolute gate and above the 20% relative gate), so the deviation is ESTABLISHED. The excess is 3.58 km, just under the 3.60 km that would have made it MATERIAL, so this is not a material deviation. I use the 10.78 km trace figure, not the rounded 10.8 km convenience copy on the trip record, which POL-RD-01 forbids for the threshold test.\n\nTrace integrity (POL-RD-07). The trace carries 169 fixes at an unbroken 10-second interval, 100% coverage, no gaps and a maximum inter-fix gap of 0 seconds. It is not impaired under limbs (a) to (c); the deviation may rest on the trace alone and no independent corroboration is required.\n\nBurden (POL-RD-08). Trip identifier TRP-00106 matches across trip_record, gps_trace and fare_breakdown, and the excess is measured from an unimpaired trace, so the rider's initial burden is discharged. The rider's profile (deviation_claims_60d of 1, substantiated 1) does not trigger the 4-or-more / 1-or-fewer corroboration rule. The burden shifted to the driver and nothing discharges it: no traffic advisory covers the trip window (EV-ADVIS-00106-01 is MISSING at weight 0.0, so POL-RD-03 is unavailable and any external-cause assertion carries no weight — POL-RD-13; neither party in fact asserts one); the single chat message is the rider's own complaint at 08:46:30 ('why we at havelock? bugis is behind us'), not an instruction, and with waypoint_hint null POL-RD-04's corroboration test cannot be run, so under POL-RD-14 the excess stands as measured; pickup_amended_at and dropoff_amended_at are both null, so POL-RD-05 does not run; fare_model is METERED with quoted_fare_sgd null, so POL-RD-11 does not run; and vehicle_type is RYDE_TAXI, so POL-RD-12's matched-itinerary baseline does not displace the 7.2 km optimal.\n\nRemedy (POL-RD-02). recomputed_fare = ((3.80 base + 0.75 x 7.2 km = 5.40 + 0.28 x 19.0 min = 5.32) x 1.0 surge, read from fare_breakdown.surge_multiplier) + 0.80 platform fee + 0.00 ERP on the optimal route + 0 fixed surcharge + 0 waiting-time fee - 0 promo = 15.32. Charged total is 26.04. Refund = 26.04 - 15.32 = 10.72, above the SGD 0.50 de minimis floor and 41.17% of the charge, below the 90% that would promote it to a full refund. The payable amount rounds UP to SGD 10.75.\n\nERP (POL-RD-09). Both charged gantries are real crossings — the trace passes 0.0 m from CTE (Braddell Rd) and 24.1 m from CTE (Chin Swee tunnel), inside the 250 m match radius — and neither lies on the optimal route (optimal_route_erp_sgd 0.00). The 5.50 of off-route ERP is therefore already comprehended inside the 10.72 refund under POL-RD-09(1) and is never added on top; awarding the rider the contested 26.04 would charge the driver twice for the same 5.50. No line is phantom, so no POL-RD-09(4) billing-integrity refund or referral arises.\n\nRepeat pattern (POL-RD-06). driver_profile.deviation_flags_90d is 0 against completed_trips_90d of 96, so no pattern is established and no tie-break, FULL_REFUND uplift or conduct referral follows. prior_deviation_flags is a lifetime counter and is context only under POL-GEN-01; it is not used.\n\nNo clause of this policy produces a referral on these facts, so the referrals list is empty. Confidence is 0.95, above the 0.70 floor, resting on artifacts all at weight 1.0. The monetary effect of SGD 10.75 exceeds the SGD 8.00 automatic-execution threshold, so the ruling issues and the amount is held for release rather than executed automatically (POL-GEN-05). The disputed 26.04 otherwise stands, reduced by this 10.75 refund to the rider. This matches the earlier PARTIAL_REFUND precedents sharing POL-RD-01, POL-RD-02 and POL-RD-08."
